WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:15.650
heart pounded as he sat up and looked around the stall.

2
00:00:17.071 --> 00:00:19.272
He couldn't see what had touched him in the dark.

3
00:00:19.892 --> 00:00:21.413
"Who's there?"

4
00:00:21.853 --> 00:00:25.234
Edward called out nervously, but again no one answered.

5
00:00:25.254 --> 00:00:28.776
"Whoever you are, reveal yourself.

6
00:00:29.864 --> 00:00:34.287
And if you're a ghost, well I'm not afraid of ghosts!"

7
00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.789
Edward sounded much braver than he felt.

8
00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:42.192
He wished that the mysterious creature would go away and leave him alone.

9
00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:47.295
But it startled him again, this time by slapping his arm.

10
00:00:47.315 --> 00:00:49.556
"Stop that!"

11
00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:50.857
Edward cried out.

12
00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:55.800
There was only one thing to do: touch the creature before it touched him again.

13
00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.922
Edward reached out a trembling hand and touched a long, warm tail.

14
00:01:00.942 --> 00:01:04.144
"You're not a ghost!"

15
00:01:06.806 --> 00:01:08.107
Edward laughed with relief.

16
00:01:09.387 --> 00:01:11.008
"You're just a calf!

17
00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:15.191
Lie down beside me, and we'll keep each other warm."

18
00:01:18.573 --> 00:01:21.635
With his new friend nearby, Edward felt less lonely.

19
00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:27.153
As he fell asleep, he thought about how relieved he was to be free of John and Frank.

20
00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:33.835
The next morning Edward was leaving the stall when he heard someone humming.

21
00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:39.296
Before he could hide, a little girl carrying a basket entered the barn.

22
00:01:40.877 --> 00:01:43.997
Her eyes widened with surprise when she spotted Edward.

23
00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:47.738
"You don't belong here," she said.

24
00:01:47.758 --> 00:01:49.639
"Who are you?"

25
00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:52.280
"I'm Edward, your king.

26
00:01:54.752 --> 00:01:55.412
Who are you?"

27
00:01:55.432 --> 00:02:02.256
"My name is Priscilla Grant, and I'm honored to meet you, Your Majesty."

28
00:02:03.897 --> 00:02:06.719
Priscilla put down her basket and curtsied to Edward.

29
00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:10.280
Edward was surprised at this mark of respect.

30
00:02:11.281 --> 00:02:13.682
People usually mocked him when he announced he was king.

31
00:02:13.702 --> 00:02:17.324
"What are you doing in our barn?"

32
00:02:17.744 --> 00:02:18.685
Priscilla asked.

33
00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:23.948
"We have cows and horses sleeping here, but you're our first king."

34
00:02:25.828 --> 00:02:29.470
Edward told Priscilla everything that had happened since he left the palace.

35
00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:34.213
"I can't remember the last time I had a good meal," he said.

36
00:02:34.233 --> 00:02:40.636
"We don't have much, but my mother always feeds beggars," Priscilla said.

37
00:02:40.656 --> 00:02:42.677
"Come with me."

38
00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:49.661
As he followed Priscilla to the farmhouse, Edward made a silent vow.

39
00:02:49.681 --> 00:02:57.309
"After I'm crowned, I'll always be kind to children because Priscilla helped me."

40
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.971
Mrs. Grant was surprised to have a king in her kitchen, but she welcomed Edward.

41
00:03:04.991 --> 00:03:09.972
"I pity the boy," she thought as she listened to his story.

42
00:03:09.992 --> 00:03:13.293
"There's something wrong with his mind.

43
00:03:14.413 --> 00:03:17.114
I'll find out where he belongs and send him home."

44
00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:23.296
Mrs. Grant gave Edward a large chunk of bread and told him to sit by the fire.

45
00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.082
"That's all I have right now, but lunch will be ready at noon."

46
00:03:30.704 --> 00:03:33.966
She watched the boy for a moment, wondering if he lived outside.

47
00:03:35.728 --> 00:03:36.928
Perhaps he was a shepherd.

48
00:03:40.791 --> 00:03:42.852
Priscilla found you in our barn."

49
00:03:43.953 --> 00:03:45.414
Mrs. Grant stirred some soup.

50
00:03:46.595 --> 00:03:49.136
"Do you have much experience with animals?"

51
00:03:49.156 --> 00:03:52.038
"No, not really."

52
00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:54.180
Edward swallowed some bread.

53
00:03:55.228 --> 00:03:58.912
"We have dogs and horses at the palace, but the servants take care of them.”

54
00:04:00.774 --> 00:04:02.535
At the mention of servants, Mrs.

55
00:04:02.615 --> 00:04:03.816
Grant had another idea.

56
00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.958
Maybe he was a servant.

57
00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:11.524
She talked about carrying firewood, scrubbing floors, and polishing boots.

58
00:04:12.765 --> 00:04:15.267
But Edward didn't have anything to say about those things.

59
00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:19.812
Mrs. Grant moved on to breaking eggs.

60
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.941
"You should see our head chef break eggs for chocolate cake!"

61
00:04:26.462 --> 00:04:28.122
Edward said enthusiastically.

62
00:04:28.142 --> 00:04:31.424
"She never drops any shells in the batter.

63
00:04:32.464 --> 00:04:36.586
And she makes the best pies and Mrs.

64
00:04:36.626 --> 00:04:39.507
Grant smiled as Edward described his favorite desserts.

65
00:04:39.527 --> 00:04:44.650
"He's eaten a lot of fancy foods," she thought.

66
00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:49.872
"He must be a kitchen helper, maybe even in the palace.

67
00:04:51.068 --> 00:04:53.609
I'll test him by having him wash dishes."

68
00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.972
You want me to wash dishes?"

69
00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:05.315
At first Edward was insulted, but then he remembered the family's kindness to him.

70
00:05:06.955 --> 00:05:09.196
Washing dishes might be a way to thank them.

71
00:05:11.497 --> 00:05:15.439
After Edward finished the dishes—he broke a cup and a plate—Mrs.

72
00:05:15.479 --> 00:05:16.900
Grant had more chores for him.

73
00:05:18.932 --> 00:05:23.754
That morning he learned to peel apples, sharpen knives, and sweep the kitchen floor.

74
00:05:25.555 --> 00:05:28.576
He didn't do a great job with any of these chores, but Mrs.

75
00:05:28.616 --> 00:05:29.916
Grant still gave him lunch.

76
00:05:32.077 --> 00:05:34.698
After lunch Edward was eager to be on his way.

77
00:05:35.839 --> 00:05:36.579
However, Mrs.

78
00:05:36.639 --> 00:05:40.341
Grant had other ideas and handed him a pail full of kitchen scraps.

79
00:05:40.361 --> 00:05:43.062
"Oh, I don't need more food."

80
00:05:44.102 --> 00:05:45.903
Edward tried to hand the pail back to her.

81
00:05:45.923 --> 00:05:48.164
"I'm full from lunch."

82
00:05:49.808 --> 00:05:51.710
Mrs. Grant struggled to hide a smile.

83
00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.712
"These are for the pigs, Your Majesty.

84
00:05:58.274 --> 00:06:01.617
Let's go outside, and I'll show you where the pigpen is."

85
00:06:01.637 --> 00:06:07.501
"You've been very kind to me," Edward said as they went outside.

86
00:06:08.562 --> 00:06:10.843
He was about to say that kings don't feed pigs.

87
00:06:12.344 --> 00:06:17.288
But just then he spotted two people coming up the front path—John and Frank!

88
00:06:19.064 --> 00:06:19.986
"Thank you for everything.

89
00:06:20.748 --> 00:06:21.570
I must be going!"

90
00:06:22.512 --> 00:06:24.036
Edward dropped the bucket of scraps.

91
00:06:24.056 --> 00:06:26.281
"Right now!"
